{"step_index":270,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T09:01:42Z","content":"Here are the live logs from **`th2-revproxyp-fe1`** demonstrating that the redirection and reverse proxy to Centreon Map are working:\n\n---\n\n### 1. HTTP Transaction Trace\n\nA client requesting root `/` on port `9443` receives the <span style=\"color:yellow\">**HTTP 301**</span> redirect, and following it leads straight to the Centreon Map backend which responds with <span style=\"color:green\">**HTTP 401**</span>:\n\n```http\n# Step 1: Initial request to root /\nGET https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/\nHTTP/2 301 \nlocation: https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/centreon-map/\nserver: nginx\n\n# Step 2: Redirect followed to /centreon-map/ -> Proxied to 172.30.198.50:9443\nGET https://map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443/centreon-map/\nHTTP/2 401 \nserver: nginx\ncontent-type: application/json;charset=ISO-8859-1\n{\"code\":401,\"message\":\"Full authentication is required to access this resource\"}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Live Access Log (`/var/log/nginx/extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr-9443-access.log`)\n\n```text\n[10/Sep/2026:09:00:24 +0000] \"GET / HTTP/2.0\" 301 162 \"-\" \"curl/7.74.0\"\n[10/Sep/2026:09:00:24 +0000] \"GET /centreon-map/ HTTP/2.0\" 401 80 \"-\" \"curl/7.74.0\"\n```\n\n### Log Breakdown:\n* **Line 1 (`301`)**: Root `/` hits Nginx $\\rightarrow$ Nginx evaluates `location = /` $\\rightarrow$ issues a <span style=\"color:yellow\">**301 Moved Permanently**</span> to `/centreon-map/` keeping the `:9443` port.\n* **Line 2 (`401`)**: The browser/client immediately requests `/centreon-map/` $\\rightarrow$ Nginx proxies to `https://172.30.198.50:9443` $\\rightarrow$ Centreon Map's Tomcat server responds with <span style=\"color:green\">**401 Unauthorized**</span> (requesting login credentials/token)."}
{"step_index":271,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T09:34:29Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nHere is the structure: 172.30.198.49 is the backend where the user will initiate the connection the 172.30.198.50[109.62.64.18] which is the Map. The request is sent to the reverse proxy [172.30.198.33]. Then the proxy will check for 109.62.64.18 which is DNAT onto itself. Finally the request returned to the reverse proxy and it must performed the redirection to Map. Before checking anything, show me that you understood the flow!\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-10T13:34:29+04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
{"step_index":272,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T09:34:29Z","content":"Here is my complete breakdown of your architecture:\n\n---\n\n### Architecture & Traffic Flow\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor User as User / Browser\n    participant Web as Centreon Web Backend<br/>(172.30.198.49)\n    participant FW as Firewall / VIP<br/>(109.62.64.18)\n    participant RP as Nginx Reverse Proxy<br/>(172.30.198.33)\n    participant Map as Centreon Map Backend<br/>(172.30.198.50:9443)\n\n    Note over User,Web: 1. Normal Centreon Web usage (Port 443)\n    User->>RP: HTTPS :443 (extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr)\n    RP->>Web: Proxy pass to Centreon Web (:80)\n\n    Note over User,Map: 2. Opening Centreon Map View\n    Web-->>User: Provides Map link / URL targeting 109.62.64.18:9443\n    User->>FW: Request https://map.extranetclient...:9443 (Public IP 109.62.64.18)\n    \n    Note over FW,RP: 3. Firewall DNAT Translation\n    FW->>RP: DNAT 109.62.64.18:9443 -> 172.30.198.33:9443\n\n    Note over RP,Map: 4. Reverse Proxy Routing & Redirection\n    RP->>RP: Matches server_name & port 9443<br/>Redirects / to /centreon-map/\n    RP->>Map: Proxy pass to https://172.30.198.50:9443/centreon-map/\n    Map-->>RP: Returns Map application response / API stream\n    RP-->>FW: Sends response back\n    FW-->>User: Delivers Centreon Map interface to the user\n```\n\n---\n\n### Step-by-Step Breakdown\n\n1. **User & Centreon Web (`172.30.198.49`)**:\n   * The user is logged into the Centreon Web interface (`extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr` on port `443`).\n   * When the user clicks on the **Map** module, Centreon Web references the Map server via its configured external address: **`109.62.64.18:9443`** (or `map.extranetclient.outremer-telecom.fr:9443`).\n\n2. **The Firewall DNAT (`109.62.64.18:9443` $\\rightarrow$ `172.30.198.33:9443`)**:\n   * The request for `109.62.64.18:9443` arrives at the firewall perimeter.\n   * The firewall performs Destination NAT (**DNAT**), translating the public destination IP `109.62.64.18` to the internal IP of the reverse proxy: **`172.30.198.33` on port `9443`**.\n\n3. **The Reverse Proxy (`172.30.198.33`)**:\n   * The packet lands on your reverse proxy `th2-revproxyp-fe1` on port `9443`.\n   * Nginx terminates the TLS connection, matches the virtual host, handles the root path redirect to `/centreon-map/`, and forwards the request internally.\n\n4. **The Target Centreon Map Server (`172.30.198.50`)**:\n   * Nginx proxies the traffic locally over the private network to the actual Map server at **`https://172.30.198.50:9443/centreon-map/`**.\n   * Centreon Map (Tomcat) serves the view, widgets, and WebSocket data back through Nginx to the user.\n\n---\n\n### Crucial Network Checkpoint for this Flow\n\nIf the connection is initiated by **the user's browser**, it follows standard external inbound DNAT.\n\nHowever, if **Centreon Web (`172.30.198.49`) itself** makes direct server-to-server API calls to Map using the public IP `109.62.64.18:9443`, the Firewall must support **Hairpin NAT (NAT loopback)** so that an internal host (`172.30.198.49`) can reach a public VIP (`109.62.64.18`) that loops back to an internal host (`172.30.198.33`).\n\nThe flow is understood. What would you like to inspect or verify next?","thinking":"**Deconstructing Network Request Flow**\n\nThe user describes a network flow involving a backend, a map server (potentially with a public IP), and a reverse proxy. The request originates at the backend, goes to the map server through the reverse proxy, and is then redirected back through the proxy. Understanding the DNAT aspect is crucial; the reverse proxy appears to be handling this translation. The overall path appears to be backend -> reverse proxy -> map server (DNAT) -> reverse proxy.\n\n\n**Summarizing The Request Flow**\n\nThe user initiates a request from Centreon Web, which is then directed through a firewall's DNAT rule, changing the destination IP to the Reverse Proxy's internal IP. The Reverse Proxy terminates the SSL/TLS connection and then redirects the request, which appears to be hitting the Centreon Map service. This confirms the initial understanding of the data flow.\n\n\n"}
