{"step_index":274,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T09:36:23Z","thinking":"**Verifying connection failure cause**\n\nThe user reports a failed connection to a specific IP address and port from the backend. This aligns with previous predictions. Now checking if the issue occurs when the Centreon Web instance attempts a direct connection. This test determines if the failure is systemic or specific to a certain connection pathway.\n\n\n**Investigating Hairpin NAT configuration**\n\nThe goal is ensuring Hairpin NAT functions correctly, allowing internal hosts to access a service via a public VIP that resolves back internally. Testing this requires checking connectivity from the backend host to the public VIP and observing traffic on the reverse proxy.  Asymmetric routing within the same subnet is a potential pitfall; packets might not return via the expected path.\n\nRunning a packet capture on the reverse proxy while the backend initiates the connection to the public VIP will confirm whether traffic is routed through the firewall. Lack of traffic on the reverse proxy or packets bypassing the firewall indicates an issue with Hairpin NAT or firewall rules. SSH access to the internal backend must be verified first to rule out basic connectivity problems.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"~/.ansible/kssh -u superuser 172.30.198.49 \"id\"","Cwd":"/home/koby","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Running command","toolSummary":"Test SSH to 172.30.198.49"}}]}
